                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why to reboot BMC in this case? Nothing got removed... why the system needs to be recovered?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-tool/src/vpd_tool.cpp",
                    "line": 1381,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "branupama"
                    },
                    "message": "As we are stopping the vpd-manager service before removing symbolic link, in case sym link remove fails we should go for reboot so that system will come with vpd-manager on reboot.\n\nand in any failure case, we are informing the user to go for reboot, so added this line."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-tool/src/vpd_tool.cpp",
                    "line": 1381,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Rebooting the BMC is an expensive operation. Why don't we re-start VPD-Manager in case there is a failure in removing the symlink and log that the complete process failed because of blah blah...\nIn case there is a failure in re-starting VPD-Manager, then user should be asked to reboot the BMC as firmware failed to reestablish the system into correct state."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-tool/src/vpd_tool.cpp",
                    "line": 1381,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Anupama B R",
                        "email": "anupama.b.r1@ibm.com",
